---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and conditions (draft)"
  description={`Draft terms page for ${site.name}. Not a contract and not a claim of legal compliance.`}
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="legal-draft">Draft</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This page is a draft. It is not a contract, it is not legal advice, and it does not claim compliance with any
        law.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What this page is for</h2>
      <p>
        A finished terms page would explain that each project is governed by a written scope, not by the marketing
        text on this website. That scope would say what is being delivered, what is not included, and what support
        covers. None of that is in force from this draft.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site does not offer guarantees, unlimited work, or a public price. Nothing here creates an obligation to
        start work. A qualified adviser should review the finished terms before they are published.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/contact">Back to contact</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
